<title>GERMANY: Commerzbank says can raise stake in BRE.</title>
<headline>Commerzbank says can raise stake in BRE.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Commerzbank AG said on Friday it can increase its 32.8 percent stake in Warsaw-based bank Bank Rozwoju Eksportu SA (BRE) to 48.8 percent providing it gains the approval of the Polish authorities.</p>
<p>Commerzbank chief executive Martin Kohlhaussen told shareholders at Friday's annual general meeting that BRE's shareholders had on Wednesday authorised BRE's board to issue up to 4.5 million new shares with a six-month option for Commerzbank.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
